Z||000000||batboy||12-04-1999||11:36 AM||||Todd Rundgren is a famous rock star, both with his solo career and as the leader of the group called Utopia. Three of his top radio hits from yesteryears are: "We Gotta Get You a Woman" (my theme song), "I Saw the Light" and "Hello, It's Me." Anyway, I belong to his fan club which has a special members only chat room on the 'net. Todd even pops on rare occassions to chat with you too. One of the hard core fans told me last night that Todd Rundgren used to own a Fiero several years ago and that somewhere there is a pic of Todd in the car. I'm hot on the trail for that pic, I gotta have it for my webpage.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sage||12-04-1999||03:47 PM||||Hey, I remember Todd Rungdren!  He was from Cleveland.  Do you remember the albumn he did in his basement studio where he played all the instruments and did all the vocals and most or all of the tunes were Hendricks stuff?  He (Todd) was one of the first rock people to build his own studio in his house!  Haven't heard anything from or about him for years, wondered what ever happened to him?! Thanks for the update.  Would love to see that pic you are talking about too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||12-04-1999||04:19 PM||||Yeah, I think you mean the "Runt" album where he did everything himself. I don't remember him doing an all Hendricks album, but he did one, "Deface the Music" which was a satire on the Beatles. Since this is not Fiero related, if anyone wants to, they can email me and I'll give them some URL addresses for official Todd Rundgren webpages and ones maintained by fans. I sent an email to Todd this morning, but he doesn't always answer fan's emails, the guy is kind of busy and probably gets hundreds of emails a day. The hard core fan that told me about the Fiero is supposed to try tracking it down too. Let's keep our fingers crossed.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||12-04-1999||05:29 PM||||One of my favorite songs back in the early 80's was "Hammer in my heart". GOOD TUNE!||||reg||6
Z||000004||theogre||12-04-1999||07:17 PM||||As I recall T.R. is also a programmer and produced a package of screen savers for macintosh years ago.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||12-04-1999||08:43 PM||||Yes, Todd was and is still very heavily into the computer scene, especially Macs. He was one of the first music artist to make an enhanced music CD (which combines music and computer data so if used on a CD-ROM it plays videos and has other visual effects things).<P>"Hammer In My Heart" is a great tune. Another more recent song people may of heard is "Bang a Drum All Day." He was the producer of numerous albums/CDs for other bands too. Meatloaf's "Bat Out of Hell" and Grand Funk Railroad's "American Band" are two famous albums I can think of off the top of my head.<P>Well I did get one email just now about the Todd's Fiero. A fan wrote me and believes he might of saw that pic in a old fan magazine called Utopia Times, so I might be on the right trail.||||reg||1
